        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Define and finalise rotation, expiry, and inspection procedures",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 211931,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, following up on our layout discussion, I've created the first drafts for the stock rotation procedure (A2) which covers T3, and the daily/weekly inspection checklist (A4) for T5. Please review and share your thoughts.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "A4",
              "T3",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "page_facing_up",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 314783,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "The checklist in A4 seems very long. Do we have to check everything on this list every single day?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 211931,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "@314783 Good question. It's split into two parts. The 'Daily Check' section is just a quick 5-minute scan for cleanliness, obvious stockouts, and hazards. The more detailed 'Weekly Check' section is for the full stock rotation and expiry date review.",
            "mentions": [
              314783
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 362964,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "This is a very thorough start, thank you. I have one suggestion for the rotation procedure in A2. For certain refrigerated medications and high-risk sterile supplies, a weekly expiry check isn't frequent enough. I'd recommend we create a 'Critical Item' category that requires a daily expiry check.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 446674,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "I was thinking the same thing. That's a crucial point for patient safety and compliance. We definitely need to add that category.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 211931,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Excellent feedback. I'll update A2 immediately to include a 'Critical Item' category with a daily check requirement. Based on this, let's formalize the frequencies. Proposal for D5: Daily expiry checks for 'Critical Items', weekly for all other medical supplies, and monthly for low-turnover retail products. Do we all agree?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 515752,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Agreed. That sounds like a robust system.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 446674,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Yes, I agree. That covers our risks well.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 314783,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Ok, so just the critical things every day. That makes sense.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 211931,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Great, D5 is locked in. Now for the inspection checklist, A4. I've incorporated the daily/weekly split we discussed. Any other feedback before we approve it?",
